export anchor ScorecardStyle:
    number: 209
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Scorecard
    idea: A board report you can work from, where every figure sits on a ruled row beside its target, drawn as a bullet chart with a red target tick, so the page answers whether the team is meeting its numbers.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #f6f6f3, the page behind the report
        paper: #ffffff, the top bar, tables and the style sheet
        inkNavy: #14213d, text, actual bars, the primary button and heavy rules
        sub: #4a5468, notes, column heads and dates
        rule: #d5d6d0, row rules and field borders, never text
        bandPoor: #c5cad3, the poor range of a bullet and last week bars
        bandFair: #dadde3, the fair range of a bullet and initials squares
        bandGood: #eceef1, the good range of a bullet
        targetRed: #b42318, target ticks, the Missed result and the overdue line
        metGreen: #166534, the Met result and positive variance
        nearAmber: #8a4b00, the Near result
        focusBlue: #1d4ed8, the focus outline
    type:
        One stack, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Liberation Sans,
        sans-serif, with tabular figures everywhere. The greeting is 30px
        bold tracked tight, actual figures 26px bold, body 15px, section
        labels 13px bold caps tracked 0.1em and column heads 12px bold caps
        in the sub colour.
    layout:
        A white top bar edged by a 2px navy rule holds a small square
        brand mark and Brightwork, a horizontal text nav whose current item
        has a 3px navy underline, then a square search field, a navy New
        project button, a square bell with a red dot and Mara Okafor with
        initials. Under it a 1216px column opens with a caps eyebrow giving
        Weekly scorecard and the date, the greeting, a red square with 4
        tasks are overdue, and a legend for actual bar, target tick and
        ranges on the right. The first section is a scorecard table with
        the columns Measure, Actual, Target, Against target, Variance and
        Result. Its five rows are tasks completed this week 73 against 59
        or more, overdue tasks 4 against 0, hours logged 186 against a 200
        hour target, tasks due this week 23 against 73 or fewer, and
        projects on track 4 against 6, each with a full width bullet chart
        of grey ranges, a navy actual bar and a red target tick. The second
        table lists the six projects with status, a percent bullet with the
        target tick at 100 percent, tasks, due date, days left and tasks
        needed per day. Last comes a two to one row with a grey and navy
        daily column chart crossed by a dashed red line at last week's
        average of 8.4 a day, beside a ruled activity list with initials
        squares and times. Below 860px the nav becomes a scrolling row and
        the search hides. Below 700px each table row becomes a stacked
        block with small labels before each figure.
    spacing: An 8px unit. Rows have 14px padding, sections sit 40px apart, a 24px gutter and 16px on phones.
    density: Medium. One measure per row with actual, target, chart, variance and result side by side.
    corners: Square everywhere, including buttons, fields, initials and status marks.
    borders: 1px warm grey rules between rows. A 2px navy rule under the top bar and under every section label.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Thin square capped line icons at text size. Results and statuses
        use filled shapes, a circle for Met and On track, a triangle for
        Near and At risk, and a square for Missed and Behind, always with
        the word.
    focus: A 2px focus blue outline offset 2px. A focused row gets a pale blue fill.
    tone: Plain and numerate like a finance pack, such as Team measures this week and Needed per day.
